{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let Reuben live, etc., and let his men be a number, etc.</b> The verse's saying ״יְחִי רְאוּבֵן״ — our Sages of blessed memory said (Sifrei Devarim 343) that he prayed for Reuben, that he should have a portion in the World to Come. And perhaps it is possible to say that it refers to the great ones of the tribe who died in the assembly of Korah, as they said of blessed memory (Bemidbar Rabbah 18:3) that the two hundred and fifty men were all heads of sanhedrin, and some were of the tribe of Reuben, as they said of blessed memory (Rashi on Numbers 16:1). And since there is grounds to say that the assembly of Korah has no portion in the World to Come (Sanhedrin 109a), for this he prayed ״יְחִי רְאוּבֵן״ — meaning his tribe; and even though they were only two hundred and fifty men, since they were its great ones, the entire tribe may be designated by them." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that he is speaking about Reuben himself, but it is for his own sake, for when the branches of the great ones of the tribe are lopped off, it diminishes, on the side of the righteous who is Reuben, his eye — therefore he prayed that he would live in the World to Come. And this accords with the opinion of the one who says (Sanhedrin 108a) that the assembly of Korah does have a portion in the World to Come." "<b>And let his men be a number.</b> He prayed for them that they should be righteous, for their roots were scorched in the stumbling of their great ones in the affair of Korah, as stated above. Therefore he prayed ״וִיהִי מְתָיו מִסְפָּר״ — meaning, after the manner of what they said of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 26a), that Hezekiah said before the Holy One, blessed be He, ״רַבִּים אֲשֶׁר אֶת שֶׁבְנָא״ etc., and the Holy One, blessed be He, replied: the wicked have no count. Therefore Moses said in the sweetness of his expression ״מְתָיו מִסְפָּר״ — meaning, that they should not be wicked, for then they have no count. And the prayer of a righteous person is effective for this matter, by the sod of ״צַדִּיק מוֹשֵׁל בְּיִרְאַת אֱלֹהִים״ (II Samuel 23:3; cf. Shabbat 63a):"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:00.775294393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}